 "W4": "A4 = 2T/{+-1} = (Z/2)^2 x| Z/3; on the three parity lines (one per non-zero parity, h^1(F; chi) = 1) the (Z/2)^2 acts by the three non-trivial characters and the 3-cycle permutes them: the standard 3-dimensional irreducible representation of A4 (its character (3, -1, 0, 0) has norm 1); for an involution it splits 1 + 2 -> 1 + 1 + 1 over C. Representation theory, no computation."
}